WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.030
As you have ordered, we have made the changes to the Kanto region's A and B Block lineups.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.270
But what is the purpose of this?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.450
You don't understand?

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:22.660
I see.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:28.380
You've moved Teikoku Academy from B Block to A Block so that they can crush Raimon.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.480
This will be interesting.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.590
Teikoku Academy?

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.080
No way!

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.080
Seriously?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.350
That doesn't make sense!

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.420
We were supposed to be up against Aoba Academy for the semi-finals!

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.880
We're doomed.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.900
We were notified this morning that these Block divisions were "revised to reflect its current standing."

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:39.010
Isn't it more like they just went and changed Aoba and Teikoku around?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.700
They went out of their way to change the Blocks just to have us go against Teikoku Academy.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.760
There goes the end of our winning streak.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:47.310
But wait!

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.810
We don't know that until we actually play!

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:54.050
Teikoku Academy is under the hands of Fifth Sector now.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.530
They've got a whole slew of Avatar users on their team.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.340
It's useless.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.610
Fifth Sector's gotten serious on us. It's all over.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:06.730
But isn't it awesome that we get to fight against Teikoku Academy?

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.520
Raimon versus Teikoku... I'm so excited!

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.290
But we'll have to fight against Teikoku with only ten members.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:20.170
Minamisawa-san left the team, and Tsurugi hasn't been coming to practice.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.930
If you just think about it normally, there's no chance for us to win.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.140
We should find another person to join.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.140
No, we're fine like this.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.370
We'll work with the ten members here!

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:35.550
Captain...

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.130
Well said, Shindou.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:40.230
We'll charge towards victory with the team members here now!

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.240
Yes, sir!

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:48.190
Teikoku Academy certainly isn't an opponent to take lightly.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.290
We'll need plans to go up against them.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.110
Coach, I have an idea.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:55.380
What is it, Shindou?

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.380
I'd like to try using Ultimate Thunder.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.930
Ultimate Thunder!

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.030
The hissatsu tactics?

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.310
Hissatsu tactics?

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.360
We came up with it with Coach Kudou back in the day.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.930
If we use that, we should be able to break past Teikoku's ironwall defense.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:21.210
But we've never been able to succeed in using it no matter how many times we tried.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:25.990
And it's difficult if you don't have a striker who's strong enough to handle it.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.790
Yes, we haven't been able to succeed in using it so far.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.410
But I want to give it a try!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.460
It's the only thing we've got to show Teikoku a thing or two.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.670
Okay, let's try it!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.650
Sure!

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.970
All right, I'm fired up!

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.800
What formation are we going with?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.480
We'll use the same formation as before.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.830
The first kicker is Hamano.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:50.480
Please.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.270
Sure!

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.480
Second is Hayami.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.280
Okay.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:54.730
Kirino.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.790
Is your leg okay?

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.230
Yeah.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.810
Okay, then you're third.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.680
Leave it to me!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.790
Fourth is Amagi-san!

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:05.610
Got it!

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.690
I wonder what kind of hissatsu tactics it is!

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.160
I'm getting all excited about it!

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.580
Here I go!

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.960
Why is Captain going back?

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.490
Hayami!

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:26.970
Kirino-kun!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.510
They're bringing the ball back to the defense!

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.600
Amagi-san!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.530
But it looks really impressive!

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.150
Shindou!

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.020
Watch out!

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.520
Ultimate Thunder!

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:47.950
Captain!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:49.770
Shindou!

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:51.840
It's no good.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.940
I can't take the power in the ball.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.420
I knew it.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:57.800
One more time!

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.120
I'll do it this time.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.550
Okay, it's yours.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.210
In positions, guys!

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.460
Sure thing!

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.720
It looks like this team has finally come together.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.870
Coach Endou.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.370
It's the data on Teikoku Academy.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:20.380
Yes...

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.440
Wasn't Kidou supposed to be playing on Italy's national league?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:31.150
I hadn't been able to get in contact with him lately, so I'd been wondering...

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:33.820
But I never thought something like this would happen.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:42.430
Kurama!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.550
Damn it, I can't kick it back!

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.750
Even Kurama can't do it...

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.080
But...

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.510
If even Captain and Kurama-san can't do it...

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.430
Just what kind of ball is it?

00:06:55.190 --> 00:07:00.590
Ultimate Thunder is a hissatsu tactics that gathers a tremendous amount of power into the ball,

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.800
which is then unleashed on the opponent's defense in order to break through.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:08.540
The ball accumulates energy as it gets passed around...

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:12.550
And then that ball is kicked into the dead center of the defense.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.610
It tears apart the opponent's defense.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.900
After that, you score in with a shoot.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.570
But kicking the powered-up ball at the end is the tough part.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:28.920
The last player needs extraordinary kick power to handle it.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.210
If I only had more power...

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.400
Me too.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.310
Kurama and Shindou focus more on technique than power for their shoots, after all.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.230
Tsurugi...

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:47.230
Tsurugi would probably be able to handle that ball.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.570
I don't want to admit it, but that guy's power is way above ours.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:58.370
Tsurugi...

00:07:58.370 --> 00:07:59.950
But he's not coming.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:06.550
He's probably in a lot of trouble for standing up against Fifth Sector when he's a Seed.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:22.040
<i>If you disobey our orders again,</i>

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:25.480
<i>your brother will lose his one and only hope.</i>

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.650
<i>I have faith in you.</i>

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:33.030
<i>Prove to me your true intentions in the next match.</i>

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.560
Halt!

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.440
First team, line up.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.960
Our next opponent is Raimon Jr. High.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:08.440
Yes, sir!

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:12.340
Raimon has been our rival for many a year.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.170
In other words, we were destined to fight!

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:14.820
Yes, sir!

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:17.970
Winning is our fate.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.770
Never forget that!

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:20.650
Yes, sir!

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:22.480
As you were. Return to practice.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.110
Yes, sir!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.370
Start your sit-ups!

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.880
It's been a while...

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:53.660
Endou.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:09:59.540
Kidou...

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.780
Why did you become Teikoku's coach?

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:09.410
Since Endou is Raimon's coach, what's so strange about me becoming Teikoku's coach?

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:14.070
I've heard that Teikoku is under Fifth Sector's control.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:17.040
Kidou, are you and Fifth Sector-

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:20.010
Soccer is in need of management.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.940
Endou, you'll surely understand that in due time.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:24.250
Nii-san, I can't believe you'd say that!

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:26.740
The times have changed.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.390
Soccer has changed as well.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.260
It hasn't changed!

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:31.760
Soccer is still soccer.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.730
It's meant to be played fun, freely, and seriously!

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.740
Then let me ask...

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.240
Was soccer before the existence of Fifth Sector correct?

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.230
Wins and losses in soccer are decided on the field.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:48.810
No matter the situation, playing soccer when the outcome is decided from the start is just wrong!

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.280
You of all people should know that!

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.460
You're as passionate as ever, Endou.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.320
But passion by itself won't change the world.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:04.760
If you insist that your soccer is correct, prove it on the field.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:11.220
Although I don't believe Raimon has the means to stand a chance against Teikoku in the first place.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.400
Wait, Nii-san!

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.680
He's not here...

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.320
Tenma, what're you doing?

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.190
Practice is starting.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:33.830
Go on without me.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:35.790
Trying to skip out?

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:37.680
I'm not!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.830
Well, that's not in your character anyway.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.000
Have you seen Tsurugi?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:41.950
Tsurugi-kun?

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.050
He just left.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.210
Where did he go?

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.970
Which way...

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.080
That way...

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.310
I think.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:56.370
Does he know where Tsurugi lives?

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:57.270
Dunno...

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:08.740
Tsurugi!

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.400
Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.960
Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:32.640
Tsurugi...

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:40.400
You don't have to come visit me every day, you know.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.530
Don't let me eat up so much of your time.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.400
It's no problem, Nii-san.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.240
His brother?

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.410
Don't you have practice?

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.560
You've been going on a winning streak.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:52.400
The semi-finals is next, right?

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.930
I hope you can make it to the Nationals tournament.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.100
Yeah...

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.470
What's wrong?

00:12:58.470 --> 00:12:59.590
You seem depressed lately.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:01.910
I'm fine.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.800
I'm going out for some water.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:04.970
U-Um...

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:06.620
You...!

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:06.970
You're...

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:09.260
Sorry for intruding!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.220
I'm a first-year at Raimon's soccer club, Matsukaze Tenma.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.620
So you're Kyousuke's teammate?

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:15.710
Yes.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:16.690
I hope you're getting along with him.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:20.130
Y-Yes, actually I came for Tsurugi to-

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.470
Come on, get out of here already!

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:22.580
O-Okay...

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.030
What're you trying to pull?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.780
I saw you on the street, so...

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.290
So you followed me?

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:33.410
Sorry.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:36.220
Is your brother okay?

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:40.250
Were you not coming to practice so you could look after him?

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.720
Don't butt into my business.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.500
Our opponent for the semi-finals was changed to Teikoku Academy.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.970
All the upperclassmen were saying Fifth Sector planned it that way.

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:55.490
Teikoku Academy is different from all the others we've faced.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:58.450
Everyone on the team is doing everything they can to find ways to win!

00:13:58.450 --> 00:13:59.780
So what?

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.780
Ultimate Thunder!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.150
It's a hissatsu tactics we need to win!

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:07.460
Ultimate Thunder?

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.430
But we need your power for it.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:12.740
That's what Captain said!

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.440
Why should I care?

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:18.490
But you helped us in the match with Mannouzaka!

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:19.540
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:23.910
I was just in the mood for it in that match.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:26.170
I'm not interested in teaming with you guys for real.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:26.900
Tsurugi!

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:30.420
There are things in this world you can't do anything about!

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.890
Guys like you just never get it!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.020
Tenma hasn't come back yet...

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:50.120
Where the heck did he run off to?

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:55.830
Tenma!

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.290
Did you find Tsurugi-kun?

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:01.180
Yeah.

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:07.420
What happened with Tenma?

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:10.060
You're late.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.120
Sorry.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.430
What is it?

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:17.420
Coach, I couldn't bring Tsurugi back.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:20.710
I wanted to play soccer with him...

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.060
If you're feeling down, go practice.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.150
They're all really pumped for it!

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:26.510
Hayami!

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.140
Kirino-kun!

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.590
Amagi-san!

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.150
Shindou!

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:35.000
Ultimate Thunder!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.430
Captain!

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:45.610
All right, again!

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:46.090
Yeah!

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:47.990
Captain...

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:51.890
Practicing is what makes "cannot do" into "<i>can</i>  do".

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.200
Look, Shinsuke's at it too!

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.730
Full Throttle Jump!

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.600
That was a pretty good shoot!

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:10.890
But you'll be up against Teikoku Academy.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.410
You'll need to improve your precision.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.030
Okay!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.700
Shinsuke...

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.320
Tenma, you go too.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:18.790
Okay!

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:21.470
I'll work on Soyokaze Step!

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:23.990
No, you should practice shoots.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.370
Me, shoot?

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:28.960
With your passion, anything's possible.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.130
Anything?

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:34.410
You don't have to be held to just offense or defense.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.890
I'd like for you to try all sorts of things.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.930
Not held to any position...

00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:45.870
Besides, Ultimate Thunder has a weakness of bringing a striker to the back of the formation.

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:50.400
We need as many people as we can to make the finishing move.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.860
Okay then! I'll try it!

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:56.750
Score some and scare the socks off Teikoku Academy!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:57.270
Okay!

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:58.990
Shinsuke!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.080
Let's practice together!

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:02.950
Okay!

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.850
The semi-finals are coming up,

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:08.980
but without Tsurugi-kun, we'll only have ten members.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.290
I'll go meet with Tsurugi-kun.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:15.840
Leave him alone for a while.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.320
Tsurugi has his own ways of fighting.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.540
Aoyama.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.680
Ichino!

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:35.950
So you came too.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.640
Yep.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.110
So you were curious too.

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:41.500
They're up against Teikoku Academy, after all.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.660
Can Raimon win as they are now?

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:52.570
It's the first match of the Holy Road Kanto district semi-finals!

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:57.720
With a sudden Block change, the new cards reveal Raimon Jr. High versus Teikoku Academy!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:02.640
How will both teams handle the unexpected change of events?

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:07.640
I, Kakuma Ayumu, will be commentator for this passionate match today!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.650
Teikoku Academy has sure changed.

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.690
Yes, they're like an army now.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:20.350
And Nii-san seems like a completely different person...

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:27.370
What? Raimon only has ten players!

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.360
And the forward Tsurugi is absent from the roster!

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.710
With no reserve players, Raimon will have it tough today!

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:37.180
They're sure underestimating us if they're only using ten players.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.380
Don't let it get to you.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.130
We only have to think about winning.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:41.890
Roger.

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:45.490
We're really playing with just ten people...

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:49.080
And we never succeeded with Ultimate Thunder in the end.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.600
Will we be okay?

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.640
No idea.

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.120
We've done all we could.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.380
All that's left is to have faith in ourselves and fight.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:01.600
And there are a lot of times when it works out in-game when it doesn't during practice.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:02.820
Yeah!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.840
If we try our best, we'll surely find a way!

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:08.200
It'd sure be easy if things were that simple.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:13.680
Either way, these guys look far more powerful than the others we've fought.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.540
Come, Endou.

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:23.540
Use everything you've got.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.770
Raimon starts the game at kickoff!

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.650
Teikoku's 2-top, Mikado and Itsumi, are approaching!

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.570
Hamano-senpai!

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:40.990
Shindou!

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:42.410
They took it!

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.770
Asukaji steals the ball from Hamano and brings it to Itsuki!

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:48.240
With long, consecutive passes, Mikado takes the ball!

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:51.080
He blows past the defense!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.530
This is Teikoku Academy...

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.840
Their movements are completely different from the teams before.

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:58.340
Raimon's in a tight spot early in the game!

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.010
Mikado shoots!

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:07.560
Burning Catch!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.720
He blocks it!

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:16.990
Sangoku stops Mikado's shoot with his full body!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:20.460
Raimon might have a little something in them after all.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:22.050
This looks interesting.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:24.710
Sangoku-san!

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:26.290
I'm fine.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:27.400
Good block.

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:31.950
But Sangoku-san won't be able to take too many of those shoots.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.210
We'll have to focus more on defense.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:37.340
No, we'll focus on attacking.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:42.170
We'll have a better fighting chance if we attack rather than let them have their way with us!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.630
The match resumes!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.000
Shindou has the ball!

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:45.830
Tenma!

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:46.550
Okay!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:50.590
God's Baton!

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.350
Kurama!

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.100
Shindou makes his orders!

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.330
There it is!

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:01.190
Good one!

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.490
Make it in!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.910
What? Damn it!

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.290
This is Teikoku Academy's defense!

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:56.500
Teikoku's soccer is far beyond what we imagined.

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:59.890
Their terrifying Avatars and hissatsu shoots corner in Raimon!

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:04.130
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 Hair-Rising! Teikoku Academy!!

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:05.860
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:17.870
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:26.210
Practicing is what makes "cannot do" into "<i>can</i>  do".

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:26.920
That's all!
